        "problem": "Express $\\frac{-2{x}^{2}+19x+30}{(x-2)(x+1)(3x+4)}$ as a sum of partial fractions.\n\n| $\\frac{-2{x}^{2}+19x+30}{(x-2)(x+1)(3x+4)}=\\,$ | {{field-1}} | $-$ | {{field-2}} | $+$ | {{field-3}} |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $x-2$ |  | $x+1$ |  | $3x+4$ |",
        "worked_solution": "Our task is to find $A,$ $B,$ and $C$ such that\n\n$$\n\\frac{-2{x}^{2}+19x+30}{(x-2)(x+1)(3x+4)}=\\frac{A}{x-2}+\\frac{B}{x+1}+\\frac{C}{3x+4}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $(x-2)(x+1)(3x+4)$ gives\n\n$$\n-2{x}^{2}+19x+30=A(x+1)(3x+4)+B(x-2)(3x+4)+C(x-2)(x+1).\n$$\n\nFor $x=2,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2(2)^{2}+19(2)+30 & =A(2+1)(3(2)+4)+B(2-2)(3(2)+4)+C(2-2)(2+1) \\\\ 60 & =30A \\\\ A & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=-1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2(-1)^{2}+19(-1)+30 & =A(-1+1)(3(-1)+4)+B(-1-2)(3(-1)+4)+C(-1-2)(-1+1) \\\\ 9 & =-3B \\\\ B & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=-\\frac{4}{3}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{(-\\frac{4}{3})}^{2}+19(-\\frac{4}{3})+30 & =A(-\\frac{4}{3}+1)(3(-\\frac{4}{3})+4) \\\\  & \\,\\,+B(-\\frac{4}{3}-2)(3(-\\frac{4}{3})+4) \\\\  & \\,\\,+C(-\\frac{4}{3}-2)(-\\frac{4}{3}+1) \\\\ \\frac{10}{9} & =\\frac{10}{9}C \\\\ C & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{-2{x}^{2}+19x+30}{(x-2)(x+1)(3x+4)}=\\frac{2}{x-2}-\\frac{3}{x+1}+\\frac{1}{3x+4}.\n$$",
